    // SP-122 — THE RACK. Every check below reads a real capture of the Studio rack's Flash Images
    // row; every one has been shown FAILING on a real capture of the opposite state, and both
    // fractions are recorded in spine-tasks/SP-122-rack-presentation/record.md.
    //
    // TOLERANCES ARE SIZED BELOW 10 ON PURPOSE, and this is the tolerance rule in its natural
    // habitat. RadioButton.rack-row:pointerover is #FF241E2A (MainWindow.axaml:98-100), 11/10/11
    // from the rack's #FF19141F ground, and the selected fill #FF2A2130 is 17/13/17 from that same
    // ground. At the rail-door precedent of 24 the ground check would pass with the mouse merely
    // RESTING on the row, and the fill check would pass on an unselected row. Measured, not
    // supposed: the unselected strip scores 0.0000 against #2A2130 at tolerance 16 and 1.0000 at
    // tolerance 20. The right precedent here is dashboard-background's 8, not rail-door's 24/32.
    //
    // The two #2A2130 checks go tighter still, to 4, because their nearest neighbour is the
    // HOVERED row at only 6/3/6 away — RackPresentationTests.NoRackCheckAcceptsTheColourOfAnother-
    // RackState asserts that separation mechanically, so widening any of these back reddens the
    // floor and names both colours. It costs nothing: these regions are flat fills that measure
    // 7605/7605 and 36/36 EXACT, with no antialiasing in them at all.
    //
    // TWO LIMITS OF THE DOT PAIR, STATED HERE BECAUSE THEY ARE NOT VISIBLE FROM THE ROWS BELOW.
    // (1) rack-row-dot-off reads the open row's fill showing THROUGH a hollow ring, so it also
    // passes if the dot is not rendered at all. Only rack-row-dot-armed constrains that the dot
    // exists. (2) Ellipse.dot strokes #FF6B5B73 and Ellipse.dot.armed fills AND strokes the same
    // colour (MainWindow.axaml:386-389), so rack-row-dot-armed separates a filled disc from a
    // 1-DIP ring by AREA alone — 0.714 against 0.224. Its minPixelFraction is therefore the whole
    // bite, and RackPresentationTests.EveryRackThresholdSitsBetweenTheFractionsItsOwnCaptures-
    // Produced pins every threshold strictly between the two fractions its real captures scored.
    {
      "name": "rack-row-unselected-ground",
      "surface": "rack-row",
      "state": "unselected",
      "evidenceClass": "presentation-verified",
      "kind": "region-color",
      "region": { "rect": { "x": 0.45, "y": 0.15, "w": 0.42, "h": 0.7 } },
      "expectedColor": "#19141F",
      "tolerance": 6,
      "minPixelFraction": 0.98
    },
