    // SP-132 -- THE GOON PAGE. The first checks in this manifest that read pixels the PRODUCT DID
    // NOT PAINT: a payload page rendered by a real WebView2 inside the Goon practice host, driven
    // there by real input (Play door, then PRACTICE) and confirmed through UIAutomation before any
    // pixel was taken. Every fraction below is measured; the captures are named in
    // spine-tasks/SP-132-goon-evidence/record.md.
    //
    // WHAT `first-run` IS, EXACTLY, because the name has to be honest. The page's screen id is
    // `title` (ui/router.js:222 writes it onto the document element) and over it sits the title
    // screen's explainer card, which auto-opens 420 ms after the first mount on a store that has
    // never seen it (ui/screens/title.js:157). That card is what these checks photograph. The BARE
    // title menu is a DIFFERENT state, it is NOT captured here, and it is not reachable from this
    // harness without driving input INSIDE the page -- which nothing here does.
    //
    // THE TOLERANCES WERE MEASURED AGAINST THREE REAL WRONG CAPTURES AND AGAINST EVERY OTHER
    // COLOUR THIS MANIFEST DECLARES. The wrong captures are (1) the boot LOADER, from a build
    // whose manifest send was seeded out so the page never settles -- the state a capture would
    // photograph if the handshake failed; (2) the typed payload-missing surface, produced by
    // renaming payload/goon in the build output, with no source change at all; and (3) a real
    // capture of the DASHBOARD, a different surface entirely. Both checks score 0.0000 on all
    // three.
    //
    // (3) IS THE ONE THAT CHANGED THESE NUMBERS, and it is recorded because assuming it would have
    // shipped the defect. The first draft pinned the backdrop at tolerance 8, and at 8 it PASSED
    // the dashboard capture 1.0000 -- dashboard-background is #141018, only 7 away per channel. A
    // check that accepts a photograph of a different window is the defect this project has found
    // fourteen times. Both tolerances now sit strictly below the distance to the NEAREST colour
    // any other check in this file declares (backdrop: 6 against 8; card: 8 against 11), and
    // GoonServingTests.NoGoonCheckAcceptsTheColourOfAnotherDeclaredState asserts that mechanically
    // over the manifest itself, so widening either one reddens the floor and names both colours.
    //
    // A FOURTH REGION WAS MEASURED AND REJECTED, recorded because it is the whole reason to
    // measure: the scrim at the left margin (0.02, 0.35, 0.12, 0.30) is perfectly flat and scores
    // 1.0000 on the real capture -- and 1.0000 on the LOADER too, at every tolerance down to 4. It
    // cannot tell the two apart, and it would have looked exactly like coverage.
    {
      "name": "goon-page-backdrop",
      "surface": "goon-page",
      "state": "first-run",
      "evidenceClass": "presentation-verified",
      "kind": "region-color",
      "region": { "rect": { "x": 0.30, "y": 0.02, "w": 0.40, "h": 0.035 } },
      "expectedColor": "#1C0B1F",
